{
  "_comment": [
    "Level-0 atlas taxonomy: the coarse, human-designed categories.",
    "These are designed by hand rather than clustered, because k-means over a global corpus",
    "would never produce a Turkish administrative-legal category. It is small globally and",
    "large in the market this tool was built for.",
    "Category ids are APPEND-ONLY and must never be renumbered or reused. They are part of the",
    "fingerprint schema, so adding a category is a schema change.",
    "Fine-grained regions are fitted by k-means WITHIN each category, which is what keeps",
    "language from consuming the region budget: once you have conditioned on topic, there is",
    "much less room left for language to be the dominant axis of variation."
  ],
